# Dev server: one shared instance

Multiple agent sessions work in this repo at once. They have repeatedly killed each
other's servers and corrupted each other's builds. Follow these rules.

## Reuse the server that already exists

There should be exactly one dev server for this project. Check before starting
anything:

```bash
lsof -nP -iTCP:3000,3100 -sTCP:LISTEN
```

If something is listening, **reuse it** — do not start a second server. It already
serves your changes, because `next dev` hot-reloads from the same working tree.
Only start one if nothing is listening.

## Never use pkill

```bash
pkill -f "next dev"      # ❌ kills every other session's server too
pkill -f "next-server"   # ❌ same
```

This is the single biggest cause of servers dying mid-session. If a restart is
genuinely required, kill only the specific PID bound to the port:

```bash
kill "$(lsof -t -nP -iTCP:3000 -sTCP:LISTEN)"
```

## Start it with an isolated build directory

```bash
NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next-dev npm run dev
```

`next build` wipes `distDir`, so a dev server sharing the default `.next` dies
mid-session with `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` on `.next/server/webpack-runtime.js`, or every
route failing to prerender with `TypeError: e[o] is not a function`. Pointing dev
at `.next-dev` leaves `.next` free for builds. `next.config.mjs` reads
`NEXT_DIST_DIR` and `tsconfig.json` already includes `.next-dev/types/**/*.ts`.

With that in place, builds are safe to run at any time and need no coordination:

```bash
npm run build   # writes .next, exports to ./out, leaves the server untouched
```
